    <string name="s_5596cfde" formatted="false">1 reading</string>
    <string name="s_c70fa2d7" formatted="false">3 readings</string>
    <string name="s_c51cb22c" formatted="false">Reading %ld</string>
    <string name="s_b9b19c0d" formatted="false">Each reading is saved separately. Enter the values for each measurement.</string>
    <string name="s_474ab8c3" formatted="false">Assigned automatically when saved using the Android’s local time: morning before 14:00 and evening from 14:00. Saved readings can only be deleted.</string>
    <string name="s_dcae2004" formatted="false">Continued</string>
    <string name="s_31d56f75" formatted="false">The history could not be read. The original file is preserved; recover it before saving new readings.</string>
    <string name="s_70e0bf52" formatted="false">Systolic (upper)</string>
    <string name="s_71b6689a" formatted="false">Diastolic (lower)</string>
    <string name="s_657e10b6" formatted="false">Above reference</string>
    <string name="s_774e9b2c" formatted="false">Below reference</string>
    <string name="s_71502458" formatted="false">What these values mean</string>
    <string name="s_adb167a4" formatted="false">Systolic is pressure when the heart contracts. Diastolic is pressure between beats; “lower” does not mean the value is low.</string>
    <string name="s_6dd12efc" formatted="false">Adult home reference: systolic 135 or above, or diastolic 85 or above (mmHg). Assess the average over several days, not a single reading. If repeated, consult a clinician; do not change medication yourself. Your targets may differ. Not for children or pregnancy.</string>
    <string name="s_7a8bd5e7" formatted="false">Very high reading. With chest pain, shortness of breath, weakness or trouble speaking, call emergency services immediately. Without symptoms, repeat after at least 1 minute; if still this high, contact a clinician as soon as possible.</string>
